THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS

The compiled binary links Go modules published by their own authors under
their own licenses, mostly the MIT, BSD and Apache-2.0 licenses. Those terms
govern those components. The exact list, with versions and licenses, is in the
software bill of materials attached to every release, and in go.mod.

lyna-tmux can install and run codediff.nvim
(https://github.com/esmuellert/codediff.nvim), which is published by its
authors under the MIT License, at a pinned and checksum-verified release. It
is downloaded on request by `lmux review install`, into lyna-tmux's own
data directory, and it is not bundled in lyna-tmux releases. Your own Neovim
configuration and plugin directories are never touched.

lyna-tmux runs tmux (ISC License) and Claude Code, neither of which is
included in this repository or in its releases.
